#: kdegames/kolf/tutorial.kolf:61
msgid "Comment=<h3>Welcome</h3> to the tutorial course for Kolf!"
msgstr ""

#: kdegames/kolf/tutorial.kolf:110
msgid ""
"Comment=To hit the ball, press and hold the Down Arrow or left mouse button. "
"How long you hold down the mouse button or key determines strength of the "
"shot."
msgstr ""

#: kdegames/kolf/tutorial.kolf:159
msgid ""
"Comment=To aim the putter, press the Left (rotate counterclockwise) and "
"Right (rotate clockwise) Arrow keys or use the mouse."
msgstr ""

#: kdegames/kolf/tutorial.kolf:260
msgid ""
"Comment="
"<h3>Bridges</h3>Bridges can have walls on the top, bottom, left, or right."
msgstr ""

#: kdegames/kolf/tutorial.kolf:376
msgid ""
"Comment="
"<h3>Everything</h3>Here's a hole that has it all. Have fun with "
"Kolf!<br><center>-- Jason Katz-Brown</center>"
msgstr ""

#: kdegames/kolf/tutorial.kolf:483
msgid ""
"Comment="
"<h3>Slopes</h3>Slopes are slanted areas of ground that push the ball in the "
"direction that they slope. This direction is shown when you choose "
"<u>Hole->Show Info</u>."
msgstr ""

#: kdegames/kolf/tutorial.kolf:531
msgid "Comment=Hit the ball onto the slope and let it roll into cup."
msgstr ""

#: kdegames/kolf/tutorial.kolf:599
msgid "Comment=Try out these different types of slopes."
msgstr ""

#: kdegames/kolf/tutorial.kolf:731
msgid ""
"Comment=The steepness of a slope is shown when you choose <u>Hole->Show "
"Info</u>. Steepness goes from 8 (steepest) to 1 (shallowest)."
msgstr ""

#: kdegames/kolf/tutorial.kolf:805
msgid "Comment=<h3>Walls</h3>Bounce the ball off of the red walls."
msgstr ""

#: kdegames/kolf/tutorial.kolf:907
msgid "Comment=<h3>Sand</h3>Sand is yellow, and slows your ball down."
msgstr ""

#: kdegames/kolf/tutorial.kolf:956
msgid ""
"Comment="
"<h3>Puddles (Water)</h3>Hitting into a puddle (blue) adds a penalty stroke "
"to your score, and your ball is placed outside the puddle."
msgstr ""

#: kdegames/kolf/tutorial.kolf:1019
msgid ""
"Comment="
"<h3>Windmills</h3>Windmills (brown base with moving arm) have brown walls "
"(or half walls). The windmill arm's speed may vary by hole."
msgstr ""

#: kdegames/kolf/tutorial.kolf:1094
msgid ""
"Comment="
"<h3>Black Holes</h3>Black Holes transport the ball to their exit, and eject "
"it at a speed directly relational to the speed your ball was going. Choose "
"<u>Hole->Show Info</u> to see which Black Hole goes to which exit and the "
"direction the ball will come out at."
msgstr ""

#: kdegames/kolf/tutorial.kolf:1172
msgid ""
"Comment="
"<h3>Floaters</h3>Floaters are moving platforms that carry a ball that lands "
"on it. Floaters' speeds vary."
msgstr ""

